s\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#exportConversationAsMarkdown\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleExport\"\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"invariants\": [\n    \"Only app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts changes in production code; test changes stay confined to app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts, where acceptance cases are added and no existing case is deleted or weakened.\",\n    \"The '- ' list marker keeps originating inside formatCitation (as the valid paths at exportMarkdown.ts:35 and :58 already emit); formatSources keeps its '**Sources:**' header and newline join (exportMarkdown.ts:63) unchanged, so valid entries are not double-marked.\",\n    \"The fixed fallback returns keep the valid paths' line structure: one '- ' item line, then the snippet blockquote as an indented continuation '\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' with the two-space indent, so multi-citation exports remain one coherent markdown list.\",\n    \"Both console.warn diagnostics keep firing with their exact current messages ('[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \\\"...\\\"') on both degraded YouTube branches; the invalid-URL message is asserted verbatim by the existing test at exportMarkdown.test.ts:223-225.\",\n    \"Exact glyphs and formats are preserved: em-dash '—' (U+2014) as the separator before the range, en-dash '–' (U+2013) inside the 'M:SS–M:SS' range produced by the unchanged formatTimestamp.\",\n    \"The empty-snippet early return (exportMarkdown.ts:22) stays ahead of every branch, so the fixed fallbacks always interpolate a non-empty snippet.\"\n  ],\n  \"adrs\": [],\n  \"history\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"Static trace of the current tree (all verified by reading the files): formatCitation (app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts:21-59) has five returns. (1) :22 empty/whitespace snippet -> ''. (2) :32 Dynamous with empty lesson_url -> 'title — range\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' — keeps the snippet but LACKS the '- ' marker. (3) :35 Dynamous with lesson_url and (4) :58 valid YouTube -> '- [title](url) — range\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' — the correct shape. (5) :46 unparseable video_url and :53 video_url without v param -> 'title (timestamp link unavailable) — range' — LACKS both '- ' and the snippet blockquote; both warn via console.warn with the same message text. The fix is confined to returns :32, :46, :53. The only production caller chain is formatCitation <- formatSources (:63, joins entries with '\\\\n' after a '**Sources:**' header) <- exportConversationAsMarkdown (:66) <- ChatArea.tsx#handleExport (app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx:613-623, wrapped in try/catch with a toast). formatSources' newline join is why a missing '- ' marker makes the degraded entry merge into the previous list item when rendered. Citation type (app/frontend/src/lib/api.ts:46-79): snippet is required string, source_type? is 'youtube' | 'dynamous' | string, lesson_url? optional — the type needs no change. MISSION.md:39-43 ('RAG responses with rich citations': every cited chunk shows video title, link, timestamp deep-link, quoted transcript snippet) is the mission invariant the export currently violates on the degraded paths. No docs/agents/*.md or ADR covers exports or citations (searched; no docs/adr/ directory exists, no 'ADR-N' matches repo-wide). Test-file facts the implementer needs: the existing invalid-URL case at exportMarkdown.test.ts:215-227 ('should fall back to title-only with unavailable text when URL is invalid') asserts the warn message verbatim at :223-225 — its assertions still pass post-fix but its name becomes stale; it may be renamed, not weakened. The no-v-param case at :229-235 and the Dynamous-empty-lesson_url case at :260-272 already exist and must keep passing. New fallback tests should spy and silence console.warn (vi.spyOn(console, 'warn').mockImplementation(() => {})) as :216 does, since the fixed fallbacks still warn. Repro/red is deferred: on the unchanged tree the suite is green, so the AC-1 red carrier must be a NEW toContain assertion of the '  > \\\"Relevant text\\\"' blockquote (a bare startsWith('- ') boolean assertion would print no received string); its vitest failure output prints today's exact return, whose tail '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' is the promised repro symptom. Unicode trap: new assertions must type the U+2014 em-dash and U+2013 en-dash exactly — an ASCII hyphen would silently assert the wrong characters.\"\n}\n"},"design.json":{"sha256":"e1ec44db7cfbba8f6cc94351fcca40f53aaeea0576ee9259b40bbda2b282f854","text":"{\"ac_mapping\":{\"AC-1\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"AC-2\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"AC-3\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"AC-4\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"AC-5\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"AC-6\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"AC-7\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"AC-8\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"]},\"allowed_new_files\":[],\"context_sha256\":\"95a429ad83b9ce778171fcde885fb999ace4ad3aa87e72d3e915f4d177be6a2f\",\"contract_sha256\":\"2c71ef4d9ad8558f2b8922bcfcc7f19d779ccf393b8e2e29be894a8f22a22e9c\",\"data_flows\":[\"Citation (empty/whitespace snippet) -> formatCitation -> '' (early return, exportMarkdown.ts:22)\",\"Citation (youtube, valid video_url with v param) -> formatCitation -> '- [title](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ID&t=Ns) — M:SS–M:SS\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' (unchanged, guard AC-5)\",\"Citation (youtube, unparseable video_url) -> formatCitation -> '- title (timestamp link unavailable) — M:SS–M:SS\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' plus console.warn invalid-URL message\",\"Citation (youtube, video_url without v param) -> formatCitation -> '- title (timestamp link unavailable) — M:SS–M:SS\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' plus console.warn no-v-param message\",\"Citation (dynamous, non-empty lesson_url) -> formatCitation -> '- [title](lesson_url) — M:SS–M:SS\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' (unchanged, guard AC-6)\",\"Citation (dynamous, empty lesson_url) -> formatCitation -> '- title — M:SS–M:SS\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' (no link: output contains no '](')\",\"Citation[] -> formatSources -> '\\\\n\\\\n**Sources:**\\\\n' + formatCitation entries joined with '\\\\n' (unchanged)\"],\"invariants\":[\"Every degraded fallback return in formatCitation begins with '- ' and ends with the snippet blockquote continuation '\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' (two-space indent) — the same shape the valid paths at exportMarkdown.ts:35 and :58 emit (AC-1..AC-4).\",\"Valid-path returns stay byte-identical to today: '- [Test Video Title](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=abc123&t=10s) — 0:10–0:20\\\\n  > \\\"Test snippet text\\\"' for YouTube and '- [Test Video Title](https://community.dynamous.ai/c/module-1/lessons/123) — 0:10–0:20\\\\n  > \\\"Test snippet text\\\"' for Dynamous (guards AC-5/AC-6).\",\"The Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback adds only the '- ' prefix — no link target is fabricated; its output contains no '](' (AC-3).\",\"console.warn keeps firing on both degraded YouTube branches with the exact current messages ('[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \\\"...\\\"'); warnings are neither removed nor reworded (guard AC-7).\",\"Empty or whitespace-only snippet returns '' before any branch (early guard at exportMarkdown.ts:22 stays first; guard AC-8).\",\"Exact glyphs preserved: em-dash '—' (U+2014) as the separator before the range, en-dash '–' (U+2013) inside 'M:SS–M:SS' from the unchanged formatTimestamp.\",\"formatSources and exportConversationAsMarkdown are untouched — the '**Sources:**' header and newline join stay as-is, so the '- ' marker is never doubled and multi-citation exports remain one coherent markdown list.\"],\"modules\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"planned_files\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts\",\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts\"],\"public_interfaces\":[\"formatCitation(citation: Citation) -> string\"],\"seams\":[\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"design.raw.json":{"sha256":"5fb146d93b8d8ae37baaedca0823c9c1f279384464fef8b0ebefe023ce2d032e","text":"{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"modules\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"\n  ],\n  \"seams\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"\n  ],\n  \"public_interfaces\": [\n    \"formatCitation(citation: Citation) -> string\"\n  ],\n  \"invariants\": [\n    \"Every degraded fallback return in formatCitation begins with '- ' and ends with the snippet blockquote continuation '\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' (two-space indent) — the same shape the valid paths at exportMarkdown.ts:35 and :58 emit (AC-1..AC-4).\",\n    \"Valid-path returns stay byte-identical to today: '- [Test Video Title](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=abc123&t=10s) — 0:10–0:20\\\\n  > \\\"Test snippet text\\\"' for YouTube and '- [Test Video Title](https://community.dynamous.ai/c/module-1/lessons/123) — 0:10–0:20\\\\n  > \\\"Test snippet text\\\"' for Dynamous (guards AC-5/AC-6).\",\n    \"The Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback adds only the '- ' prefix — no link target is fabricated; its output contains no '](' (AC-3).\",\n    \"console.warn keeps firing on both degraded YouTube branches with the exact current messages ('[exportMarkdown] Skipping timestamp link — invalid video_url: \\\"...\\\"'); warnings are neither removed nor reworded (guard AC-7).\",\n    \"Empty or whitespace-only snippet returns '' before any branch (early guard at exportMarkdown.ts:22 stays first; guard AC-8).\",\n    \"Exact glyphs preserved: em-dash '—' (U+2014) as the separator before the range, en-dash '–' (U+2013) inside 'M:SS–M:SS' from the unchanged formatTimestamp.\",\n    \"formatSources and exportConversationAsMarkdown are untouched — the '**Sources:**' header and newline join stay as-is, so the '- ' marker is never doubled and multi-citation exports remain one coherent markdown list.\"\n  ],\n  \"data_flows\": [\n    \"Citation (empty/whitespace snippet) -> formatCitation -> '' (early return, exportMarkdown.ts:22)\",\n    \"Citation (youtube, valid video_url with v param) -> formatCitation -> '- [title](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ID&t=Ns) — M:SS–M:SS\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' (unchanged, guard AC-5)\",\n    \"Citation (youtube, unparseable video_url) -> formatCitation -> '- title (timestamp link unavailable) — M:SS–M:SS\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' plus console.warn invalid-URL message\",\n    \"Citation (youtube, video_url without v param) -> formatCitation -> '- title (timestamp link unavailable) — M:SS–M:SS\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' plus console.warn no-v-param message\",\n    \"Citation (dynamous, non-empty lesson_url) -> formatCitation -> '- [title](lesson_url) — M:SS–M:SS\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' (unchanged, guard AC-6)\",\n    \"Citation (dynamous, empty lesson_url) -> formatCitation -> '- title — M:SS–M:SS\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' (no link: output contains no '](')\",\n    \"Citation[] -> formatSources -> '\\\\n\\\\n**Sources:**\\\\n' + formatCitation entries joined with '\\\\n' (unchanged)\"\n  ],\n  \"ac_mapping\": {\n    \"AC-1\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-2\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-3\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-4\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-5\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-6\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-7\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"],\n    \"AC-8\": [\"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts#formatCitation\"]\n  },\n  \"planned_files\": [\n    \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts\",\n    \"app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"allowed_new_files\": [],\n  \"notes\": \"Smallest deep-module design: no new module, helper, file, or dependency — the change edits the three degraded return expressions inside the existing formatCitation seam and adds acceptance cases to the existing test file. Minimal-complexity ladder stops at rung 2 (extend what exists): return :32 (Dynamous, empty lesson_url) gains only the '- ' prefix; returns :46 and :53 (unparseable video_url, missing v param) gain the '- ' prefix and the '\\\\n  > \\\"snippet\\\"' blockquote continuation. No shared return-shaping helper is introduced — the valid paths at :35/:58 already inline their returns, so three direct template literals match the surrounding idiom; extracting one would be a parallel abstraction for a single reason to change. formatTimestamp, formatSources, exportConversationAsMarkdown, the empty-snippet guard, and both console.warn calls are untouched. planned_files includes the test file because the contract mandates adding acceptance cases there (existing cases must keep passing) and the kernel refuses commits outside the planned set — it is the only non-production file; production change remains exportMarkdown.ts alone. Contract declares no dependencies, so no manifest or lockfile is planned. allowed_new_files is empty. Implementation notes for the implementer: (1) AC-1's toContain assertion of the '  > \\\"Relevant text\\\"' blockquote is the red carrier — on the unchanged tree vitest prints today's exact return, whose tail '(timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' is the repro record's promised symptom; do not rely on a startsWith('- ') boolean assertion as the red carrier. (2) Type em-dash U+2014 and en-dash U+2013 exactly in new assertions. (3) The existing invalid-URL case (exportMarkdown.test.ts:215) may be renamed since its title becomes stale, but its assertions must not be weakened. (4) New fallback tests should spy/silence console.warn as the existing ones do — the fixed fallbacks still warn (noise, not failure). (5) Deliberate ceiling, per the contract: the degraded YouTube branches keep emitting '(timestamp link unavailable)' rather than linking the bare URL — restoring some degraded link is out of scope by AC-2/AC-4.\"\n}\n"},"frontier.json":{"sha256":"f35d4e60966de2c84703c0a94a6068b6aafb694309656c0fbf7140d8d87604bd","text":"{\"accepted\":true,\"blockers\":[],\"issue\":49,\"ready\":true,\"ticket_sha256\":\"6e497a14d1983bc4b5156f3ae07bcb909f93d5b7fd6629fa267f24af73e17cbf\",\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"issue-frontier.json":{"sha256":"7a025d1ceafa0b72e4dd9959ac04ee6893c5fad7173623609224e42830c7c6a1","text":"{\"blockers\":[],\"fetched_at\":\"2026-09-10T23:20:44Z\",\"issue\":{\"body\":\"## Background\\n\\n`formatCitation` in `app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts` renders each citation in an exported conversation. Its YouTube fallback path is wrong: when `citation.video_url` cannot be parsed, or has no `v` parameter, it returns exactly\\n\\n    Test Video (timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20\\n\\nwhich (a) drops the quoted transcript snippet and (b) omits the leading `- ` list marker every other path emits, so the entry merges into the previous list item when rendered. The Dynamous path with an empty `lesson_url` keeps the snippet but also lacks the `- ` marker.\\n\\nMISSION.md \\\"RAG responses with rich citations\\\" requires every cited chunk to show its transcript snippet. The export silently loses it.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n**AC-1**\\nGiven a YouTube citation whose `video_url` is `not-a-url` and whose `snippet` is `Relevant text`\\nWhen `formatCitation` is called\\nThen the returned string contains `> \\\"Relevant text\\\"` on its own line.\\n\\n**AC-2**\\nGiven the same citation\\nWhen `formatCitation` is called\\nThen the returned string starts with `- ` and still contains `(timestamp link unavailable)` and `0:10–0:20`.\\n\\n**AC-3**\\nGiven a citation with `source_type: 'dynamous'` and an empty `lesson_url`\\nWhen `formatCitation` is called\\nThen the returned string starts with `- `, contains no `](`, and still contains its `> \\\"snippet\\\"` blockquote.\\n\\n## Files expected to change\\n\\n- `app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts` (only production file).\\n- Acceptance tests in the existing `app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts`; every current case must keep passing.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Backend, schema, dependencies, `CitationModal.tsx`, `Message.tsx`, `ChatArea.tsx`, `Sidebar.tsx`.\\n- The valid-URL and valid-`lesson_url` paths, `formatTimestamp`, the export header and filename slug.\\n\\nRepro: `cd app/frontend && bun run test src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts`\\n\",\"labels\":[{\"color\":\"5319E7\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory control state\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACyJrubg\",\"name\":\"factory:accepted\"},{\"color\":\"fbca04\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxETvQ\",\"name\":\"priority:medium\"},{\"color\":\"d73a4a\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxEUlw\",\"name\":\"type:bug\"}],\"number\":49,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"fix(export): markdown export drops the transcript snippet when a citation URL cannot be parsed\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-10T23:19:07Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ShaishiBear/dark-factory-2.0/issues/49\"},\"version\":\"1.0\"}\n"},"issue.json":{"sha256":"57080f66b6c31183a24c07c90c5cf85b9b3704b0e39b76d8da38f7e2de06dc50","text":"{\"body\":\"## Background\\n\\n`formatCitation` in `app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts` renders each citation in an exported conversation. Its YouTube fallback path is wrong: when `citation.video_url` cannot be parsed, or has no `v` parameter, it returns exactly\\n\\n    Test Video (timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20\\n\\nwhich (a) drops the quoted transcript snippet and (b) omits the leading `- ` list marker every other path emits, so the entry merges into the previous list item when rendered. The Dynamous path with an empty `lesson_url` keeps the snippet but also lacks the `- ` marker.\\n\\nMISSION.md \\\"RAG responses with rich citations\\\" requires every cited chunk to show its transcript snippet. The export silently loses it.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n**AC-1**\\nGiven a YouTube citation whose `video_url` is `not-a-url` and whose `snippet` is `Relevant text`\\nWhen `formatCitation` is called\\nThen the returned string contains `> \\\"Relevant text\\\"` on its own line.\\n\\n**AC-2**\\nGiven the same citation\\nWhen `formatCitation` is called\\nThen the returned string starts with `- ` and still contains `(timestamp link unavailable)` and `0:10–0:20`.\\n\\n**AC-3**\\nGiven a citation with `source_type: 'dynamous'` and an empty `lesson_url`\\nWhen `formatCitation` is called\\nThen the returned string starts with `- `, contains no `](`, and still contains its `> \\\"snippet\\\"` blockquote.\\n\\n## Files expected to change\\n\\n- `app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts` (only production file).\\n- Acceptance tests in the existing `app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts`; every current case must keep passing.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Backend, schema, dependencies, `CitationModal.tsx`, `Message.tsx`, `ChatArea.tsx`, `Sidebar.tsx`.\\n- The valid-URL and valid-`lesson_url` paths, `formatTimestamp`, the export header and filename slug.\\n\\nRepro: `cd app/frontend && bun run test src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts`\\n\",\"labels\":[{\"color\":\"5319E7\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory control state\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACyJrubg\",\"name\":\"factory:accepted\"},{\"color\":\"fbca04\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxETvQ\",\"name\":\"priority:medium\"},{\"color\":\"d73a4a\",\"description\":\"Dark Factory triage label\",\"id\":\"LA_kwDOT-6Wzs8AAAACzxEUlw\",\"name\":\"type:bug\"}],\"number\":49